{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And Elohim said: Nevertheless, Sarah, etc.</b> — One needs to know the reason for His saying ״אֲבָל״ (nevertheless), for it has no meaning." "<b>And it appears</b> that He intended to say to him: yes, indeed, if the granting is for you alone, you have a mouth to say that you are in doubt about Yishmael — but Sarah your wife is bearing a son, meaning: on account of Sarah's giving birth, you are not authorized to forego what belongs to another. And He was precise in saying ״לְךָ״ (for you), meaning: she shall have a son from you, in accordance with her prayer, so that all the sons she will have will be from you." "Further, it is possible to say that HaShem was insistent about his saying to Him ״יִשְׁמָעֵאל״ — that he chose Yishmael. And it may be that this was the reason that Yitzchak was given to him from the side of the feminine, which is His saying ״Sarah shall bear,״ and he suffered greatly on account of this when he bound him upon the altar, for through the binding (Akedah) the birthing soul was given to him, and Rivkah, his destined mate, was then born."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:41:41.891429812Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}